# Bottom-nav footer floor (do not regress)

Canonical: `docs/DEV.md` bug **7d** and § Native input / sideways strips.

Phone chrome `bottom_nav` (both apps): Fit maroon/navy `SolidView` → overlay tabs + `bottom_nav_scroll` (`ScrollXView`) + ‹ ›. Makepad draws the X bar **over** the bottom `bar_size` of the scroll view.

## Required

```text
bottom_nav.padding.bottom     = 0 in DSL
lift_footer_above_system_bar  = safe_area.bottom only (0 on desktop); never touch padding.top
strip inside ScrollX          bottom pad ≥ bar_size (today 8 with bar_size 4)
footer scroll_bar_x colours   dark on footer bg (not stock light handle)
```

- Scrollbar is the **bottommost** chrome — nothing (no DSL pad, no FOOTER_BOTTOM constant) under it.
- Strip bottom pad is the **bar’s lane** so chips / ‹ › stay clear of the overlay.
- Duplicate the same contract per app — no shared core.

## Forbidden

```text
❌ bottom_nav.padding.bottom = 12 (or any pad under the bar) → dead strip below scrollbar
❌ strip bottom pad 0 → chips/‹ › sunk / cropped on the window edge
❌ lift_footer writing padding.top (+ bottom) → Fit footer taller than shell slot → bottom clipped
❌ bar_size: 0 “to remove the gap” while keeping chevrons — keep the bar; fix padding instead
❌ stock light ScrollX handle on maroon/navy → reads as cream floor strip
```
